sh: use the real predicate prototypes in sh_treg_combine

sh_treg_combine.cc declares t_reg_operand and negt_reg_operand itself,
returning int.  Since GCC 12 the generated predicates return bool, so
the caller reads a full int where the callee only set the low byte.
Whether that works depends on the host compiler: built with GCC 15 on
x86-64, sh_treg_combine took ordinary register loads for inverted
T-bit stores and deleted the tst/cmp before the branch, e.g. at -O2
gcc.c-torture/execute/20071120-1.c lost all of its 5 compares.

Upstream fixed this for GCC 13 (Jeff Law, 2022-11-17: "Include
tm-preds.h, remove bogus prototypes"); it was never backported to 12.

Tested on 12.2.0, sh-elf -m2, cc1 built with host GCC 15, GDB SH
simulator, gcc.c-torture/execute (GCC 14.3 testsuite): without this
patch 113 programs abort, crash or hang at -O1 (80), -O2 (78), -O3 (74)
or -Os (88); with it they all pass.  No other run result changes, no new
compile or -O2 -g -fcompare-debug failure.

--- a/gcc-12.2.0/gcc/config/sh/sh_treg_combine.cc
+++ b/gcc-12.2.0/gcc/config/sh/sh_treg_combine.cc
@@ -37,6 +37,7 @@
 #include "cfgrtl.h"
 #include "tree-pass.h"
 #include "expr.h"
+#include "tm-preds.h"
 
 /*
 This pass tries to optimize for example this:
@@ -426,10 +427,6 @@
   return GET_CODE (p) == SET && GET_CODE (XEXP (p, 1)) == IF_THEN_ELSE;
 }
 
-// FIXME: Remove dependency on SH predicate function somehow.
-extern int t_reg_operand (rtx, machine_mode);
-extern int negt_reg_operand (rtx, machine_mode);
-
 // - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
 // RTL pass class
 
